# To move swiftly.
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[move]] forward [[quickly]] upon [[two]] [[feet]] by alternately making a short [[jump]] off either foot. {{qualifier|Compare ''[[walk]]''.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Run''', Sarah, '''run'''!}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1967|first=Barbara|last=Sleigh|authorlink=Barbara Sleigh|title={{w|Jessamy}}| edition=1993| location=Sevenoaks, Kent| publisher=Bloomsbury |isbn=0 340 19547 9| page=122| passage=Through the open front door '''ran''' Jessamy, down the steps to where Kitto was sitting at the bottom with the pram beside him.}}
##* {{seemoreCites|en}}<!-- Please no more than 3–4 quotes here, further quotes only in 'Citations' (see [[WT:QUOTE]])-->
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[go]] at a [[fast]] pace; to move [[quickly]].
##: {{ux|en|The horse '''ran''' the length of the track.}}
##: {{ux|en|I have been '''running''' all over the building looking for him.}}
##: {{ux|en|Sorry, I've got to '''run'''; my house is on fire.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|author={{w|Ed Cobb}}|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Tainted Love}}|album={{w|Non-Stop Erotic Cabaret}}|year=1965|year_published=1981|artist={{w|Soft Cell}}|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XZVpR3Pk-r8|text=Once I '''ran''' to you (I ran) / Now I '''run''' from you / This tainted love you've given / I give you all a boy could give you}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cause]] to move [[quickly]] or [[lightly]].
##: {{ux|en|Every day I '''run''' my dog across the field and back.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'll just '''run''' the vacuum cleaner over the carpet.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Run''' your fingers through my hair.}}
##* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1912|author=Sir Arthur Conan Doyle|authorlink=Arthur Conan Doyle|title=The Lost World| url=http://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/139/pg139.txt|passage=Challenger and I '''ran''' Summerlee along, one at each of his elbows, while Lord John covered our retreat, firing again and again as savage heads snarled at us out of the bushes.}}
## {{senseid|en|race}} {{lb|en|transitive|or|intransitive}} To [[compete]] in a [[race]].
##: {{ux|en|The horse will '''run''' the Preakness next year.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'm not ready to '''run''' a marathon.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[transport]] someone or something, notionally at a brisk pace.
##: {{ux|en|Could you '''run''' me over to the store?}}
##: {{ux|en|Please '''run''' this report upstairs to director's office.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} Of a means of transportation: to [[travel]] (a [[route]]).
##: ''the bus (train, plane, ferry boat, etc) '''runs''' between Newport and Riverside''
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=Karl-Heinz Reger|author2=Nelles Verlag Staff|title=Malaysia - Singapore - Brunei|publisher=Hunter Publishing, Inc|isbn=9783886189021|page=91
|text=Small planes '''run''' between Alor and Langkawi. BUS: Express busses leave the bus terminal on the corner of Jl. Langgar and Jl. Stesyen for K. Kedah, {{nb...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2013-04-15|author=Mary Ann Sternberg|title=Along the River Road: Past and Present on Louisiana's Historic Byway|publisher=LSU Press|isbn=9780807150634|page=62
|text=The first steam ferry or tug, the Little Minnie, '''ran''' the river in the 1870s. When vehicles were to cross, a barge was affixed to the Minnie to carry them. The Bella Israel, a successor to the Little Minnie, sank in 1894 and 62 Along the{{nb...}}}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[transit]] a length of a river, as in [[whitewater rafting]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1979|author=United States. Forest Service. Rocky Mountain Region|title=Piedra River: Final Environmental Impact Statement & Wild & Scenic River Study|page=74
|text=To put it frankly, if you people had to hire others to run the river and survey it for you, if, in short, you can't even '''run''' it yourself, why do think you can decide who is and who is not competent? River running, as has been{{nb...}}}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} Of fish, to [[migrate]] for [[spawning]].
## {{lb|en|American football|transitive|or|intransitive}} To carry (a [[football]]) down the field, as opposed to passing or kicking.
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 29, 2019|journal=Boston Globe|author=Chad Finn|title=24 thoughts on the Patriots’ loss to the Dolphins|url=https://www.boston.com/sports/new-england-patriots/2019/12/29/patriots-dolphins-recap-thoughts-analysis|passage=Then, on their second possession, Isaiah Ford '''ran''' for 11 yards after abandoning a flea flicker.  [...] The Patriots '''ran''' the ball just 27 times despite averaging 5 yards per carry.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To achieve or perform by running or as if by running.
